---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  sitemap.xml: the list of pages that tells search engines what to read.

  Why it's hand-written: the jekyll-sitemap plugin added a "last changed"
  time to some pages, and that time ended in the site's time zone (like
  "+01:00"). Spec doesn't want their time zone shown anywhere on the site.
  So this file lists the same pages with no times at all. Search engines
  are fine without them.

  Which pages: every web page (not data files like search.json), skipping
  any page that says "sitemap: false" and the 404 page. Then every log.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for p in site.html_pages %}
{%- unless p.sitemap == false or p.url contains "404" %}
<url><loc>{{ p.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc></url>
{%- endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for l in site.logs %}
{%- unless l.sitemap == false %}
<url><loc>{{ l.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc></url>
{%- endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
